kunzite: RedwoodGPU's buffers cached by default again (0997 had made them write-combined). Boot
#56 panicked at backboardd's first GEM buffer: gemNew -> IOBufferMemoryDescriptor::inTaskWithOptions
(kIOMapWriteCombineCache) -> memoryReferenceCreate -> mach_make_memory_entry_internal ->
pmap_set_cache_attributes_internal -> ml_static_vtop: "phystokv_range: illegal PA 0x60de0000; phys
base 0x90000000, size 0x17ff00000". A write-combined IOBMD has its pages' cache attributes changed
through the kernel's physical aperture, which covers 0x90000000 + 6 GB only, while the allocator
also hands out pages of the lower DDR bank below it: topaz's old note ("from the lower DDR bank
the kernel cannot map back") named a real hazard, only not the one it said. gpu_cached=0 still
asks for write-combined. 0997's other changes stay: the push at creation (in cached mode what it
did before), wrapDelta, read-only client memory.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/RedwoodGPU.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/RedwoodGPU.cpp
index af630f4..dd2d1b6 100644
